 "notes": "Minbu, Magwe, Pakôkku and Mandalay (first row) print 'Do.' (= Other Tibeto-Burmese languages); expanded. Upper Chindwin, Tai (Shan) mother tongue, Burma Group Females printed '31,9?6' with a broken third digit (fragments suggest 5, i.e. 31,956, but not certain); recorded as the string '31,9?6'. Continues from leaf 240. Part II Bilingualism (printed pages 234-235): rows = district x mother-tongue group; cols 3-4 total number of speakers of that mother tongue (M/F); cols 5-14 number speaking a subsidiary language in each group (M/F). No Persons column. Each row is emitted as one record per subsidiary group with non-nil figures (total_males/total_females repeat the col 3-4 totals); a row with no subsidiary figures at all is emitted once with subsidiary=null so the total is kept. Self-checks: subsidiary sums never exceed totals; totals for Burma, Karen and Tai mother tongues equal the I-D group figures for that district, and Mon-Khmer totals equal I-D Mon (K) + Palaung-Wa (L) (all pass)."
}